\section*{1. Overview}
This chapter defines a spacecraft deck layout optimized for integration of the
Continuous Yield Propulsion Core (CYPC-1). The layout organizes structural,
thermal, control, and stability subsystems around CYPC-1 while preserving
continuous-yield thrust stability and global manifold integrity.

\section*{2. Deck Zoning Scheme}
The spacecraft is partitioned into four primary zones:

\begin{enumerate}
    \item Forward Mission Deck (FMD)
    \item Central Systems Deck (CSD)
    \item Aft Propulsion Deck (APD)
    \item Stability \& Manifold Deck (SMD)
\end{enumerate}

CYPC-1 resides in the Aft Propulsion Deck as the primary thrust module.

\section*{3. Aft Propulsion Deck (APD)}
\subsection*{3.1 CYPC-1 Core Placement}
CYPC-1 is mounted on the Structural Interface Frame (SIF) at the centerline of
the APD, aligned with the spacecraft thrust axis.

\subsection*{3.2 Local Subsystems}
\begin{itemize}
    \item QP-Core chamber and gradient coils
    \item SRK structural hull and strain-sensor lattice
    \item FDE nozzle assembly and vectoring coils
    \item SFM stability sensor array and actuators
\end{itemize}

\section*{4. Central Systems Deck (CSD)}
\subsection*{4.1 Control \& Telemetry Hub}
The CSD houses:

\begin{itemize}
    \item Thrust Vector Control Grid (TVCG) controller
    \item Conservation Synchronization Bus (CSB) router
    \item Eigenvalue spectrum evaluation unit for $(K - \Gamma_P)$
\end{itemize}

\subsection*{4.2 Structural Coupling}
Load paths from CYPC-1 through the SIF are routed into the CSD primary
structure, maintaining:
\[
f_{\text{yield}} < 0
\]
for all operational thrust profiles.

\section*{5. Forward Mission Deck (FMD)}
\subsection*{5.1 Payload Isolation}
The FMD hosts mission payloads and is structurally isolated from APD thrust
vibrations via tuned damping interfaces consistent with:
\[
D \succ 0
\]
for the global damping matrix.

\subsection*{5.2 Thermal Isolation}
Thermal routing from CYPC-1 is prevented from coupling into FMD via dedicated
Thermal Regulation Network (TRN) channels.

\section*{6. Stability \& Manifold Deck (SMD)}
\subsection*{6.1 Manifold Monitoring}
The SMD contains:

\begin{itemize}
    \item Global manifold stability monitor
    \item Geometry modulation actuators
    \item Nozzle deformation and hull mode sensors
\end{itemize}

\subsection*{6.2 Stability Condition}
Deck-level integration maintains:
\[
\lambda_{\max}(K - \Gamma_P) < 0
\]
for all thrust cycles.

\section*{7. Interface Mapping}
\subsection*{7.1 Structural Interface}
APD $\rightarrow$ CSD via SIF load paths; CSD $\rightarrow$ FMD via damped
structural bridges.

\subsection*{7.2 Thermal Interface}
CYPC-1 exhaust and chamber heat routed through TRN manifolds in APD and CSD,
bypassing FMD.

\subsection*{7.3 Control Interface}
TVCG, CSB, and SMCL controllers located in CSD, with sensor and actuator lines
to APD and SMD.

\section*{8. Conservation Layer Integration}
Deck layout preserves:

\[
\nabla_\mu T^{\mu\nu} = 0, \qquad
\nabla_\mu J^\mu = 0, \qquad
\frac{dH_{\text{metric}}}{dt} \approx 0,
\]

by ensuring CYPC-1 telemetry and control signals are routed through the CSB in
the CSD, with global monitoring in the SMD.

\section*{9. Layout Summary}
\begin{itemize}
    \item CYPC-1 centralized in APD on thrust axis.
    \item Control, stability, and conservation logic centralized in CSD.
    \item Payload isolated in FMD from thrust and thermal feedback.
    \item Manifold stability instrumentation concentrated in SMD.
\end{itemize}

\section*{10. Conclusion}
This deck layout provides a structurally and dynamically coherent integration
environment for CYPC-1, maintaining continuous-yield propulsion stability while
protecting mission payloads and preserving global conservation and manifold
integrity.

